-block-cards", "dandy-columns-v2 OR value-pillars-outlined-cards", "zigzag-features OR benefits-alternating-rows", "full-bleed-split", "quote-carousel", "bottom-cta OR aurora-cta-finale"], "is_custom": false, "sort_order": 0}, {"recipe_path": "microsite", "recipe_id": "microsite-proof-led", "label": "Proof-led", "description": "a credibility-first page that leads with metrics, comparison, and customer proof", "style_notes": "Open with the account's situation, then stack evidence early: a quick credibility/metrics bar, one big highlighted number, a head-to-head old-way vs new-way comparison, the core benefits, and a real-sounding customer quote before the close. Analytical, confident tone.", "enabled": true, "updated_by": 36476, "created_at": "2026-06-28T01:42:26.20979+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-07-05T21:35:01.664887+00:00", "skeleton": ["aurora-gradient-hero OR ai-scan-hero", "trust-bar OR stat-row", "comparison", "features-spotlight-cards", "how-it-works-vertical-timeline OR how-it-works-alternating", "quote-with-image", "cta-split-image"], "is_custom": false, "sort_order": 0}, {"recipe_path": "microsite", "recipe_id": "microsite-story-led", "label": "Feature-led", "description": "a narrative page that walks the account from problem to transformation", "style_notes": "Tell one continuous story: name the problem and what it costs, agitate it briefly, then resolve with a clear numbered path to the outcome. Land on a human proof moment (the quote) and then into specific technical features (if you have enough to include use tabbed categories otherwise choose dandy columns V2. Favor depth over breadth — fewer, richer sections. If you use DSO Heartland Hero, use the full bleed one with a full bleed image.", "enabled": true, "updated_by": 36476, "created_at": "2026-06-28T01:42:19.005655+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-07-05T21:35:21.676088+00:00", "skeleton": ["spotlight-glow-hero OR aurora-gradient-hero OR dso-heartland-hero", "icon-row OR value-pillars-outlined-cards", "zi